.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd July 20, 2026
.Dt EMACS-JOURNAL-2026-07-20 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-journal-2026-07-20
.Nd working notes of 2026-07-20
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss Spell-check: switch jinx to global-jinx-mode
.Ss Summary
Applied Emacs Redux's \(dqReplacing Flyspell with Jinx\(dq https://emacsredux.com/blog/2026/07/13/replacing-flyspell-with-jinx/.
Jotain already used jinx; the missing piece was the post's central recommendation: drive jinx from
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "global-jinx-mode" Ns No "\fP"
instead of per-mode hooks.
.Ss Change
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "lisp/init-writing.el" Ns No "\fP"
— the
.Ql "jinx"
.Ql "use-package"
block replaced its
.Ql ":hook ((text-mode . jinx-mode) (org-mode . jinx-mode))"
pair with a single
.Ql ":hook (emacs-startup . global-jinx-mode)" .
Keybindings
.No \&( Ns Ql "M-$"
→
.Ql "jinx-correct" ,
.Ql "C-M-$"
→
.Ql "jinx-languages" )
are unchanged.
.El
.Ss Why
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fBOne mode replaces two.\fP
.Ql "global-jinx-mode"
subsumes both
.Ql "flyspell-mode"
and
.Ql "flyspell-prog-mode" .
Jinx decides \fIwhat\fP to check by \fBface\fP, so in a programming buffer it limits itself to comments and strings automatically — no separate prog-mode variant, no per-language hooks.
.It
\fBCode comments/docstrings are now checked.\fP The old per-mode hooks fired only in
.Ql "text-mode"
(and, redundantly,
.Ql "org-mode" ,
which already derives from
.Ql "text-mode" ).
Prose was covered; typos in comments and docstrings across every
.Ql "prog-mode"
buffer went unchecked.
Global mode closes that gap — this was Finding 4/11 of the 2026-07 deep-research review.
.It
\fBRedundant hook dropped.\fP
.Ql "(org-mode . jinx-mode)"
was a no-op on top of the
.Ql "text-mode"
hook; folding everything into the global mode removes it.
.El
.Ss Interaction with init-lang-data.el
Data/config buffers that merely \fIderive\fP from
.Ql "text-mode"
but read as code — YAML in particular — still want jinx off.
.Ql "jotain-lang-data--enable-prog-mode-features"
already turns it back off unconditionally
.No \&( Ns Ql "(when (bound-and-true-p jinx-mode) (jinx-mode -1))" ).
Ordering still holds under global mode:
.Ql "global-jinx-mode"
enables jinx during
.Ql "after-change-major-mode-hook" ,
then the mode's own
.Ql "yaml-mode-hook"
runs the opt-out afterward, so those buffers end up jinx-free exactly as before.
.Ss Docs
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/configuration/package-reference.mdx" Ns No "\fP"
— regenerated body text to match the updated
.Ql ";;; @doc"
block on the jinx form (hand-synced; no Nix in this environment to run
.Ql "just docs-refresh-packages" ).
The
.Ql "packages-doc-in-sync"
flake check compares byte-for-byte against the
.Ql "@doc"
markers, so this must track the source comment exactly.
.El
.Ss Not changed (deployment-dependent, pre-existing)
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "Jinx: No dictionaries available for \(dqen_US\(dq" Ns No "\fP"
on hosts whose enchant has no en_US backend.
Global mode surfaces this in more buffers than the old text-mode-only hooks did, but it is the same deployment gap noted on 2026-06-09 — the Nix-wrapped
.Ql "jotainEmacsPackages"
ships the dictionary; a bare host still needs a hunspell/nuspell dict on
.Ql "DICPATH" .
No config change belongs here.
.El
